Overlap the host-staged all-reduce of row-parallel layers with their GEMM (fork).

The host-staged all-reduce (host-staged-allreduce.patch) moves data on the copy
engines, so the SMs are free while it runs -- but each all-reduce waited for the
whole GEMM before it, and the next layer waited for it. With
VLLM_ALLREDUCE_HOST_STAGED_OVERLAP=N a row-parallel layer (o_proj, down_proj,
the GDN out_proj) computes its tokens in N pieces through the custom op
vllm::row_parallel_overlap (opaque to torch.compile, layer looked up by prefix)
and starts each piece's all-reduce while the next piece's GEMM runs. The backend
gets start()/finish(); all_reduce() is both. Pieces below the backend's minimum
size, CUDA-graph captures (decode) and setups without the backend fall back to
one GEMM + all-reduce. Lossless.

2x RTX 3090, TP=2, CTX=fast, INT8_ACT=int8 INT8_LAYERS=mlp, warm prefill tok/s:
  2k / 8k / 32k   off 2,670 (8k), 2,405 (32k)
  N=2             2,756 / 2,788 / 2,498
  N=4             2,581 / 2,782 / 2,543
The launchers set N=2 at --tensor-parallel-size 2.

